  "id": "photic-driving",
  "term": "photic driving",
  "definition": "Photic driving is the effect in which repetitive light flashes make brain rhythms follow the stimulation. It can involve synchronization of the rhythm to the flash rate and increased rhythm amplitude when the flash frequency matches the brain’s own natural frequency.",
